elly-halved practical cap\nbinds.)\nSTRATEGY (phased, macro headwind \u2192 do not deploy fully at T0):\n  \u2022 Tranche 1 (now): 2.0% (50% of target) \u2014 price $209.17, mid 52-wk range.\n  \u2022 Tranche 2: +1.0% on Q2 FY27 confirmation (2026-08/09): organic revenue\n    growth \u22658% ex-Informatica AND Agentforce+Data ARR \u2265$4.0B AND cRPO \u2265 +13%\n    [all [Actual] from the 10-Q].\n  \u2022 Tranche 3: +1.0% either on a pullback \u2264$195 (\u224810-yr-low multiple zone) or\n    on 10-yr yield <4.3% (macro relief).\n  \u2022 Trim to \u22642% if: 10Y >5.3%; FY28 initial guide < +5%; or two monitoring\n    gates breach. Hard stop-loss logic: thesis breach, not price.\n  \u2022 Expected hold: 3\u20135 years; review every 6 months vs Section 8 gates;\n    conviction decays \u22121/6mo absent confirming prints.\nBOTTOM LINE: A wide-moat, high-FCF franchise at a fair-not-cheap price\n(14.8x FY27 non-GAAP EPS, 15.1x EV/EBITDA), with a genuinely free agentic-AI\noption that the market prices at zero. The catch: organic growth is ~8%\n(not the 13% headline), the balance sheet is newly levered, and the macro\nregime (4.7% 10Y, sticky 3.4% CPI, tightening-bias Fed) is a headwind for\nlong-duration software. Size accordingly (4%, cap 5%), phase entries, and let\nthe KPIs \u2014 cRPO, organic growth, Agentforce ARR, SBC%, leverage \u2014 arbitrate\nbetween the $146 bear and the $314 bull.\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nEND OF ANALYSIS \u2014 RS2 v2.0\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u25