 MODEL SELECTION\nStep 0-1. Archetype: B \u2014 QUALITY COMPOUNDER.\n  Justification (3+ reasons):\n   1. Recurring subscription model: subscription & support revenue $10.6B in\n      Q1 FY27, +14% Y/Y [Actual - Q1 FY27 release]; gross margin 77.6% [Actual]\n      \u2014 a compounding, high-retention revenue base, not an option story.\n   2. FCF machine: OCF $14.996B FY26 [Actual], FCF $14.402B [Arithmetic],\n      A-FCF margin (OCF \u2212 capex \u2212 SBC) 26.2% [Arithmetic] \u2014 self-funding,\n      negative net-debt dynamics, buyback fuel.\n   3. #1 CRM share 20.0% vs #2 Oracle 4.1%, 13 consecutive years [Estimate -\n      IDC via research brief]; margin expansion 14.4% \u2192 19.0% \u2192 20.1% GAAP OI\n      margin FY24-FY26 [Actual] \u2014 classic compounder economics.\n  Step 0-2. Valuation engine: ENGINE 1 (Traditional DCF + Multiples).\n  Step 0-3. Transition check: NO archetype transition. Agentforce (agentic AI)\n    is $0.8-1.4B ARR vs $42.8B TTM revenue (~2-3%) [Actual/Estimate] \u2014 an\n    increment on the platform, not yet a hybrid hardware/platform structure\n    (criteria: Core >50% rev, GM >30%, FCF+ \u2014 already met, but the optionality\n    is <5% of revenue, so Engine 4 is NOT triggered; it is carried in scenarios).\n  Step 0-4. Why not another engine:\n   - Engine 4 (Option-Led) would over-weight Agentforce; it is 2-3% of revenue.\n   - Engine 3 (Hybrid) would misclassify: no hardware installed base.\n   - Error if wrong engine: Engine 4 would produce an IV swing of \u00b150% from\n     AI assumptions; Engine 1 anchors to cash flows actually being generated.\n\nExpected value bridge (forward, Section 4): Base IV $311 [Estimate],\n  expected value $299, MoS vs base +33% [Arithmetic].\n\nCONVICTION: HIGH (10/15). ACTION: BUY (accumulate), staged. TARGET WEIGHT: 6%.\n12-MONTH TARGET: $260-290 (+24% to +39%). 3-YEAR BASE: $311; BULL: $450.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u25