u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nStep 1.5-1. Base rates (framework reference + context):\n  - Mega-cap S&P 500 company, 10-yr survival: ~85-90% [Estimate - CRSP-style\n    survival literature].\n  - Large-cap enterprise software compounding FCF at high-single-digit for a\n    decade: ~40-50% [Estimate - most mega-caps decelerate to GDP+].\n  - Platform/monetization-model transition (seat \u2192 consumption/AI) success:\n    ~20-30% [Framework reference base rate].\n  - Cyclical peak \u2192 40% drawdown: not applicable (non-cyclical archetype).\n\nStep 1.5-2. Deviation from base rate:\n  Base success probability (~45%) is raised to ~55-60% (posterior). Company-\n  specific justification (\u22653 required):\n   1. Share dominance: 20.0% vs 4.1% for #2 \u2014 pricing + ecosystem moat that\n      most transition candidates lack [Estimate - IDC].\n   2. Transition already demonstrated in cash terms: Agentforce ARR $800M,\n      +169% Y/Y; Agentforce + Data 360 ~$1.4B ARR, +114% Y/Y; cRPO $33.6B,\n      +13-14% [Actual - Q1 FY27 release] \u2014 not a promise, a billing line.\n   3. Self-funding: 36.1% OCF margin, A-FCF 26.2%, net debt 0.6\u00d7 EBITDA,\n      $25B ASR already executed [Arithmetic/Actual] \u2014 no external capital\n      needed for the transition.\n   4. Installed base: 150,000+ customers, RPO $67.9B (+11%) [Actual/Estimate].\nStep 1.5-3. Base-rate shock check: posterior success (bull+base = 68%) vs\n  framework base for platform transitions (20-30%) exceeds 2.0\u00d7 \u2014 RED FLAG\n  REVIEW. Resolution: the framework base rate refers to pre-revenue/platform\n  greenfield transitions. Salesforce's transition