er.\n\nStep 2-2. Moat assessment + dynamics (0-3 each):\n  Intangible assets (brand): 3 (13-yr #1 CRM, \"Salesforce\" is a verb)\n  Switching costs: 3 (data, workflows, multi-cloud, training; enterprise\n    implementation $5K-$50K+ [Estimate - research brief])\n  Network effects: 2 (AppExchange/ISV ecosystem)\n  Cost advantage: 1 (premium priced, not lowest cost \u2014 HubSpot/Zoho attack\n    from below)\n  Economies of scale: 3 (150k customers; 36% OCF margin on $41.5B revenue)\n  Regulatory barriers: 1 (data-residency compliance; not a licence moat)\n  Data moat: 3 (CRM data + Data Cloud; 28.6T tokens processed, +152% QoQ\n    [Actual - Q1 FY27 call excerpt])\n  TOTAL: 16/21 \u2014 FORTRESS (upper end of Wide).\n  Moat direction: STABLE. Widening on data/AI (token volume, Data Cloud);\n  narrowing on seat economics (AI commoditization, SMB price pressure).\n  Net: Stable, with the bear case hinging on the narrowing leg.\n\nStep 2-3. Lynch classification: STALWART (10-13% growth, 20% margins,\n  buybacks, fortress economics) with fast-grower optionality (Agentforce).\n  Core checkpoints: (a) does growth stay >8% without margin collapse \u2014 YES\n  in base (Q1 FY27 +13.3% [Actual]); (b) is EPS growth > revenue growth \u2014\n  YES (+36.7% NI in Q1 FY27 [Actual], margin expansion + buybacks).\n\nStep 2-4. Financial strength scorecard [all [Actual] unless noted]:\n  - Revenue growth: FY26 +9.6%; 3-yr CAGR (FY23-FY26) +9.8%; Q1 FY27 +13.3%\n    [Arithmetic].\n  - Operating margin: FY26 20.1%; 3-yr avg 17.8% [Arithmetic].\n  - Net income: FY26 $7.457B, +20.3% Y/Y; TTM $8.023B [Arithmetic].\n  - ROE 12.6%; GAAP ROIC ~10% (goodwill-heavy); economic ROIC ex-goodwill\n    ~35-40% [Estimate \u2014 see Section 2.5].\n  - FCF margin (OCF basis) 36.1%; A-FCF (post-SBC) 26.2%; OCF/NI conversion\n    2.0\u00d7 [Arithmetic].\n  - Net debt $7.6B \u2248 0.64\u00d7 EBITDA; interest coverage 25.7\u00d7 [Arithmetic].\n  - Piotroski 7/9; accruals \u22120.07 (cash-heavy earnings) [Arithmetic].\n  JUDGMENT: EXCELLENT.\n\nStep 2-5. Capital allocation scorecard (0-3 each):\n  1. Buyback efficiency: 3 \u2014 $50B authorization Feb-2026, $25B ASR launched\n     Q1 FY27 at ~19-22\u00d7 forward earnings, below the 10-yr average multiple\n     [Actual - press reports]. Vendor share count 819M implies ~14% YoY\n     reduction [Estimate].\n  2. M&A track record: 1 \u2014 Slack ($27.7B), Tableau, MuleSoft: integration\n     absorbed, but ROIC > WACC + 3% not demonstrable; D&A still $3.6B/yr\n     [Actual/Estimate].\n  3. Capex efficiency: 3 \u2014 incremental ROIC far above WACC; FCF conversion\n     2.0\u00d7 [Arithmetic].\n  4. Mix rationality: 3 \u2014 reinvestment + buybacks + first dividend (0.9%\n     yield [Actual - vendor]) \u2014 coherent.\n  5. Guidance accuracy: 2 \u2014 FY26 guidance raised twice and delivered\n     ($41.45-41.55B) [Actual - research brief]; FY27 initial guide \"missed\"\n     aggressive sell-side (shares sank) but was then raised [Actual - Q1\n     FY27 release]. Strong but imperfect.\n  TOTAL 12/15. Insider bonus: 0 (ownership 2.99% < 5%; 6-mo insider activity\n  [Unconfirmed]). Scorecard: EXCELLENT.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2