50\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 8. MONITORING RULES\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nTHESIS INTEGRITY (quarterly, re-evaluate if breached 2 consecutive quarters\nunless stated):\n  M1. cRPO growth \u2265 8% (Q1 FY27: +13-14% [Actual]).\n  M2. Agentforce + Data-360 ARR growth \u2265 40% (Q4 FY26: +169% [Actual]);\n      token volume growth positive (Q1 FY27: +152% QoQ [Actual]).\n  M3. A-FCF margin \u2265 23% (currently 26.2% [Arithmetic]).\n  M4. GAAP OI margin \u2265 18% and on path to 22.5% by FY36 (20.1% FY26).\n  M5. SBC/revenue \u2264 9.0% (8.5% FY26); share count \u2264 900M (819M vendor).\n  M6. Revenue growth \u2265 7% (Q1 FY27 +13.3% [Actual]).\n  M7. 10Y \u2264 5.0%; if >5.2%, re-run WACC at 10.5% (IV \u2192 ~$270).\n  M8. No material breach-litigation accrual; renewal rate stable.\nPRE-MORTEM \u2014 \"If this failed by 2031, why?\":\n  P1. AI margin deflation: volume grows, dollars don't (token price \u221250%+).\n      Early warning: cRPO <8% while tokens +50% (volume without pricing).\n  P2. Strategic stagnation: growth 4-5%, buybacks at high multiples,\n      activist divestitures (e.g., Slack) fragment the platform. Early\n      warning: guidance cuts; GAAP OI margin <18%; DSO rising.\n  P3. Trust shock: breach escalates into EU/CCPA enforcement + churn.\n      Early warning: material legal accruals; CISO-switch reports; renewal\n      rate decline.\nDECISION JOURNAL (Section 11) updated at every earnings print.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 9. RED TEAM & ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nStep 9-1. SHORT THESIS (5-7 bullets, same data):\n  S1. Agentic AI destroys the seat model: customers buy outcomes, not\n      seats; Agentforce ($0.8-1.4B ARR) is 2-3% of revenue and may CANNIBALIZE\n      higher-margin seat licenses (token revenue replacing user revenue).\n  S2. Growth has already halved: FY22 +24.7% \u2192 FY26 +9.6% \u2192 the \"compounder\"\n      label rests on margin, not growth; consensus is 9.5% and decelerating.\n  S3. Margin expansion is accounting-fragile: GAAP OI margin gains come\n      partly from acquired-intangible amortization decay (D&A 8.7% of\n      revenue) \u2014 the non-cash tailwind fades; A-FCF margin is flat-to-down\n      in our own bridge.\n  S4. SBC $3.5B/yr (8.5% of revenue) is real dilution masked by buybacks;\n      buybacks funded by 2.0\u00d7 cash conversion are circular if growth fails.\n  S5. Competition is intensifying: Microsoft/Google bundle AI-CRM at the\n      platform layer; HubSpot/Zoho attack SMB pricing; 20% share vs 4.1%\n      #2 is dominance but dominance attracts attack.\n  S6. Valuation is not \"cheap\" on quality terms: 22.7\u00d7 trailing P/E with a\n      12-13% implied terminal margin means the market is NOT giving credit\n      for the AI story \u2014 the burden of proof is on the bulls.\n  S7. Overhangs: Starboard/Elliott activism, ShinyHunters breach litigation,\n      $4.0B current debt maturity at 4.7% rates, high institutional\n      ownership (88%) \u2192 ETF-flow vulnerability.\nStep 9-2. LOGIC COMBAT (1-10):\n  Long: 8.2 (cash flows, guidance, ARR, ASR, moat)\n  Short: 6.8 (model-transition risk is real, but mostly priced; several\n  bullets are about optics, not cash)\n  Gap 1.4 < 2.0 \u2192 conviction NOT downgraded (borderline \u2014 flagged).\nStep 9-3. ADVERSARIAL DATA: ShinyHunters breach (Jan-2026) [Estimate -\n  research brief]; Starboard/Elliott public pressure [Estimate]; \"17%\n  overvalued\" critique (Trefis/SimplyWallSt) [Estimate]; Truist $380\n  target (bull-side check) [Estimate]; CNBC \"shares sink on mixed\n  guidance\" [Actual - headline].\nStep 9-4. KILLED ARGUMENTS (and revival conditions):\n  K1. \"Agentforce is vaporware\" \u2014 KILLED by $800M ARR +169%, 29,000 deals\n      +50% QoQ, 28.6T tokens [Actual]. REVIVE if ARR growth <30% or token\n      volume declines 2 consecutive quarters.\n  K2. \"SBC makes cash flow illusory\" \u2014 KILLED by 26.2% A-FCF margin AFTER\n      full SBC subtraction [Arithmetic]. REVIVE if SBC/revenue >10%.\n  K3. \"Buybacks destroy value\" \u2014 KILLED by execution at ~19-22\u00d7 forward with\n      26% FCF margin and below-average multiple. REVIVE if buybacks\n      continue above 28\u00d7 with growth <5%.\n  K4. \"Bear case is a rounding error\" \u2014 NOT killed: Deep Bear $135 is a\n      coherent path (margin 18%, growth 4%). Kept at 10% probability.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n37-point audit (PASS unless noted; any FAIL would force recalculation):\nA. Methodology (1-6): 1 classification B with 3 reasons PASS | 2 engine\n   selection + alternatives rejected PASS | 3 time-point discipline (T0\n   2026-08-24 vs T-1 FY26 vs TTM Apr-26 not mixed) PASS | 4 no DCF-only\n   conclusion (multiples + reverse DCF + scenarios) PASS | 5 no peer-only\n   conclusion PASS | 6 no TAM-only conclusion (Agentforce quantified) PASS.\nB. Valuation (7-13): 7 WACC fully sourced PASS | 8 terminal g 3.5% \u2264\n   nominal GDP PASS | 9 explicit 10-yr forecast shown PASS | 10 tornado\n   top-3 identified PASS | 11 reverse DCF consistent with price PASS |\n   12 net-debt components declared, overlap flagged PASS | 13 share-count\n   discrepancy (819M vs 956M filed) carried into sensitivity, not buried\n   PASS.\nC. Bias (14-20): 14 overconfidence audited (wide 50/80% CIs) PASS | 15 base\n   rates anchored PASS | 16 success prob vs base-rate red-flag reviewed and\n   resolved PASS | 17 red team before conclusion 